, and at 22:58 the Raven's cloak lies heaped on the floor (clue 3) – yet the Raven cloak is ankle-length for Felix at 1.95 m (clue 6).", "At 22:31 the Swan is so tall that only wings and chin fit in the booth frame (clue 3) – the Swan costume was hired by Clara, 1.58 m (clue 6).", "In the cloakroom the Swan collected ticket 14 – the Raven cloak – and the Raven collected ticket 15, the Swan wings (clue 2). They swapped at 22:01–22:02.", "So tiny Clara wore the Raven, and drunk Felix spent the evening as the Swan. The letter is addressed to the author of Night Garden (clue 5) – Clara (clue 2) – and the manuscript folder is gone (clue 1)."], "cleared": ["Felix (motive: lines cut) was the tall Swan in the booth at 22:31 (clues 2, 3 and 6).", "Theo (contract cut) and Oscar were on stage from 22:30 to 23:00 in front of everyone (clue 4).", "Rosalind (row about selling the theatre) was the Cat at the bar at 22:33, and at 1.70 m the cloak would not drag (clues 3 and 6).", "Mira was at the stage door with her headset, and she is the witness (clue 6)."]}}, {"slug": "sabotage-at-the-observatory", "level": 3, "crime": "Sabotage", "who": "saboteur", "title": "Sabotage at the Observatory", "teaser": "The night before a big announcement, a telescope is wrecked and the images deleted. The log names the culprit. Too neatly.", "intro": "The night before <b>Prof Helena Ross</b> was due to announce a discovery, someone smashed the telescope's mirror cover and deleted the night's images. The control log points straight at one person. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "The night before Prof Helena Ross was due to announce a discovery, someone smashed the telescope's mirror cover and deleted the night's images. The control log points straight at one person. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "", "daily": null, "public": "2026-11-14", "suspects": [{"name": "Ada Kim", "role": "Observatory director"}, {"name": "Greta Lind", "role": "Science journalist"}, {"name": "Helena Ross", "role": "Professor of astronomy"}, {"name": "Ian Shaw", "role": "Rival astronomer"}, {"name": "Priya Nair", "role": "PhD student"}, {"name": "Tom Fletcher", "role": "Technician"}], "clues": [{"name": "Helena Ross", "role": "Professor of astronomy", "quote": "I started the telescope at twenty to eleven and drove to the village for dinner with my husband. At half past one I came back to this. Those images would have changed everything.", "label": "DAMAGE REPORT", "evidence": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px\"><div style=\"font-family: 'Special Elite', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 19px; color: #1E1B18; margin-bottom: 6px\">Damage report – main dome</div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #5C554D\">Discovered</div><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #1E1B18; line-height: 1.4\">01:30, by Prof Ross</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #5C554D\">Mirror cover</div><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #1E1B18; line-height: 1.4\">Smashed with a fire extinguisher</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #5C554D\">Images</div><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #1E1B18; line-height: 1.4\">22:40–23:10 deleted from the control computer</div></div><div 