ydia hired a small van with a roof rack and at 23:52 bought a petrol can and petrol (clue 5). Ollie saw that kind of van go up the mill lane around two (clue 6).", "So ‘asleep at home, no car’ is a lie (clue 5)."], "cleared": ["Victor raised the insurance because the bank demanded it (clue 2), his truck never moved (clue 6), and the boot print is a woman's (clue 1).", "Rosa moved her paintings because of the roof leak (clue 3) and was photographed at the gala at 02:07 and 02:15 (clue 6).", "Simon (wanted the land) was running the auction at 01:58 and 02:15 (clue 6).", "Ollie is the witness, and Hannah is the investigator."]}}, {"slug": "the-ransom-of-captain-biscuit", "level": 3, "crime": "Kidnapping", "who": "kidnapper", "title": "The Ransom of Captain Biscuit", "teaser": "The seaside theatre's famous talking parrot is snatched, and a cut-out ransom note demands £5,000. Three people had a reason – and a newspaper.", "intro": "Captain Biscuit, the talking parrot who stars in the Seaview Theatre's summer show, was taken from his cage on Saturday night. On Sunday morning a ransom note arrived. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "Captain Biscuit, the talking parrot who stars in the Seaview Theatre's summer show, was taken from his cage on Saturday night. On Sunday morning a ransom note arrived. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-14", "daily": null, "public": "2026-11-14", "suspects": [{"name": "Hugh Pembroke", "role": "Pet shop owner"}, {"name": "Ivan Petrov", "role": "Stage manager"}, {"name": "June Hart", "role": "Newsagent"}, {"name": "Maggie Doyle", "role": "Theatre owner"}, {"name": "Nell Archer", "role": "Theatre cleaner"}, {"name": "Ricky Sands", "role": "Magician"}], "clues": [{"name": "Maggie Doyle", "role": "Theatre owner", "quote": "This was pushed under my door on Sunday at seven. The letters are cut out of a newspaper. I jus