IS HIDDEN …</div>\n<div style=\"border-bottom: 1.5px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Hugo Fabre", "motive": "The rival house Orage paid Hugo €50,000 (clue 5).", "proof": ["The safe's clock was still on summer time (clue 2). The clocks went back at 03:00 (clue 1), so ‘04:35’ on the safe was really <b>03:35</b>, and it closed at 03:52.", "Hugo took a taxi to Maison Lune at 03:10, arrived at 03:25 and left at 03:58 (clue 4).", "He knows the code (clue 5). His video call at 04:15 came after the safe was closed.", "So his claim that he was asleep at home until 04:15 is a lie (clues 4 and 5)."], "cleared": ["<b>Céline</b> was on the phone at home from 03:28 to 03:52 (clue 6). Her taxi at 04:20 was too late.", "<b>Ravi</b> was at the hospital from 01:10 to 06:30 (clue 3).", "<b>Bruno, Ana and Theo</b> don't know the code (clue 1)."]}}, {"slug": "the-glasshouse-blackmail", "level": 2, "crime": "Blackmail", "who": "blackmailer", "title": "The Glasshouse Blackmail", "teaser": "A blackmail photo shows the garden director with a shop-bought prize orchid. A clock in the picture says 10:10. Look again.", "intro": "At Kingsley Botanical Gardens, director <b>Dr Ophelia Rand</b> won the orchid show. Then a blackmail letter arrived – with a photo. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "At Kingsley Botanical Gardens, director Dr Ophelia Rand won the orchid show. Then a blackmail letter arrived – with a photo. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-14", "daily": null, "public": "2026-11-14", "suspects": [{"name": "Dr Ophelia Rand", "role": "Director of the gardens"}, {"name": "Josh Weller", "role": "Delivery driver"}, {"name": "Ken Ashdown", "role": "Head gardener"}, {"name": "Mabel Fry", "role": "Volunteer guide"}, {"name": "Priya Nand", "role": "Orchid Society judge"}, {"name": "Sid Okoro", "role": "Ca