ay in (clue 3).", "The minutes show Clive out of the room from 22:35 to 22:45 (clue 5) – exactly when the candle was lit. Harriet's only break was at 21:40, far too early.", "Clive says he never left the room (clue 4) – the minutes say otherwise. The petrol can was clean and dry, a plant to frame Silas (clue 2)."], "cleared": ["Josh lied about sneaking in at 01:30 (clue 3), but the candle had been burning since about 22:40 (clue 2).", "Norah (wanted the plot, offer rejected that evening) was hosting a dinner in London from 20:10 to 00:35, two hours away (clues 5 and 6).", "Silas left at 18:02 (clue 3), and his can was a plant (clue 2).", "Harriet was out of the room only from 21:40 to 21:44, and Felicity never left (clue 5)."]}}, {"slug": "the-midnight-bagpiper", "level": 1, "crime": "Nuisance", "who": "piper", "title": "The Midnight Bagpiper", "teaser": "For three nights, someone in a kilt has played the bagpipes – badly – on the village green at 2 a.m. Little Drumley hasn't slept a wink.", "intro": "In the sleepy village of Little Drumley, a mystery piper has woken everyone at two in the morning for three nights in a row. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "In the sleepy village of Little Drumley, a mystery piper has woken everyone at two in the morning for three nights in a row. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-14", "daily": "2026-11-30", "public": "2026-11-30", "suspects": [{"name": "Angus Kilbride", "role": "Bagpipe teacher"}, {"name": "Dora Penhallow", "role": "Village shopkeeper"}, {"name": "Gita Osei", "role": "Delivery driver"}, {"name": "Hector Lamb", "role": "Farmer"}, {"name": "Ivy Crump", "role": "Drama club costume keeper"}, {"name": "Rev. Archie Bellweather", "role": "Vicar"}], "clues": [{"name": "Rev. Archie Bellweather", "role": "Vicar", "quote": "I've kept a careful log. Same tune every night – ‘Scotland the Brave’