px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Celeste Varnay", "motive": "With Pompom out of the way, Celeste's dog Bijou won the Toy Group (clue 1).", "proof": ["Celeste says she was in Ring 3 at two o'clock, as the printed programme says (clue 4).", "But Ring 3 was flooded and closed until 14:45, and the Toy Group was moved to 15:00 (clue 2). So her alibi is a lie.", "At 13:55 she bought a sausage roll she didn't eat and asked the way to the hay store (clue 5).", "Pompom was found in the hay store with sausage-roll crumbs on her whiskers (clues 1 and 6)."], "cleared": ["<b>Duncan</b> is the false lead: his crate held his own white puppy, Pompom was still on her bench as he left, and he was with the vet from 14:02 to 14:40 (clues 3 and 6).", "<b>Lady Hortensia</b> was at the tea tent (clues 3 and 5). <b>Barney</b> served alone all afternoon (clue 5).", "<b>Pam</b> was at the stewards' desk (clue 3), and <b>Rupa</b> was with Snowy in the vet tent (clue 6)."]}}, {"slug": "the-ghost-train-takings", "level": 3, "crime": "Theft", "who": "thief", "title": "The Ghost Train Takings", "teaser": "£3,200 vanishes from a locked ghost-train booth, and a ghoul's mask lies on the floor. Two people had keys, and two wore high-vis.", "intro": "On the busiest night of <b>Merriweather's Travelling Funfair</b>, Saturday's takings vanished from the locked ghost-train ticket booth. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "On the busiest night of Merriweather's Travelling Funfair, Saturday's takings vanished from the locked ghost-train ticket booth. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-14", "daily": "2026-11-29", "public": "2026-11-29", "suspects": [{"name": "Fenella Rook", "role": "Fortune teller"}, {"name": "Glenn Harrow", "role": "Security guard"}, {"name": "Maud Merriweather", "role": "Fair owner"}, {"name": "Pip