win it by cheating.", "proof": ["Rex's car 7 is a 1925 Morris Bullnose with a top speed of 45 mph (clue 5). Yet it covered the 40-mile route from 13:30 to 14:20 – 50 minutes, an average of 48 mph (clues 4 and 6). Impossible: Rex did not drive the whole route.", "From Mill Bridge (13:41) the old farm track leads straight back to the showground in 3 miles (clue 6) – and the marquee stands beside that track (clue 1).", "At 14:02 a dark green open car stood on the farm track behind the marquee with its number hidden (clue 2). Car 7 is the dark green one (clue 5). The trophy vanished between 13:55 and 14:10 (clue 1).", "The missing Kestrel Inn stamp proves nothing for Rex – the marshal was having tea (clue 3)."], "cleared": ["<b>Ivy</b> has a grudge against Rex, but her car was stamped at Kestrel Inn, 34 miles out, at 14:40 (clue 4).", "<b>Wally</b> was in the Kestrel Inn from 13:51 to 14:08 (clue 3). <b>Hugh</b> was on the main gate from 14:00 (clue 1).", "<b>Margot</b> was in the commentary box until she found the theft, and <b>Nina</b> was with the judges (clue 2)."]}}, {"slug": "the-opera-house-tiara", "level": 2, "crime": "Theft", "who": "thief", "title": "The Opera House Tiara", "teaser": "A diamond tiara disappears from the star's dressing room during Act 2. A patron heard a glorious aria. Did he?", "intro": "At the <b>Royal Calder Opera House</b>, a diamond tiara worn in La Traviata was stolen from the star dressing room during the second act. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "At the Royal Calder Opera House, a diamond tiara worn in La Traviata was stolen from the star dressing room during the second act. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "added": "2026-11-17", "daily": "2026-12-20", "public": "2026-12-20", "suspects": [{"name": "Clara Venn", "role": "Understudy"}, {"name": "Elena Rossi", "role": "Soprano"}, {"name": "Lord Ashcombe", "role": "Patron, Box A"}, {"name": "Peg Holloway", "role": "Dresser"}, {"name": "Sid Kemp", "role": "Usher, box corridor"}, {"name": "Tom Ruiz", "role": "Stage manager"}], "clues": [{"name": "Peg Holloway", "role": "Dresser", "quote": "I left the tiara on its stand at ten to nine and took the wig box down to the wardrobe store. When I came back at five past nine the stand was empty.", "label": "THEFT REPORT", "evidence": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px\"><div style=\"font-family: 'Special Elite', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 19px; color: #1E1B18; margin-bottom: 6px\">Theft report – star dressing room</div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #5C554D\">20:50</div><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #1E1B18; line-height: 1.4\">Peg leaves the tiara on its stand</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #5C554D\">20:51–21:04</div><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #1E1B18; line-height: 1.4\">Wardrobe store book: P. Holloway in and out, signed by the wardrobe mistress</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #5C554D\">21:05</div><div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; color: #1E1B18; line-height: 1.4\">Tiara found missing</div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 12px; padding: 5px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #D8D0C2\"><div style=\"width: 150px; flex-shrink: 0; font-family: Inte