, then scan the code to name the culprit.</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; width: 250px\">\n<div style=\"font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: #5C554D\">NEXT CLUE IS HIDDEN …</div>\n<div style=\"border-bottom: 1.5px dashed #1E1B18; height: 30px\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>"}], "solution": {"killer": "Sandra Hughes", "motive": "Sandra wanted the £300 console for herself (clues 5 and 6).", "proof": ["The console was there at 14:28 and the box was empty at 16:00 (clues 1 and 5).", "Sandra says she was on the cake stall all afternoon (clue 2). But she is not on the cake stall rota (clue 2), the tombola rota puts her on the tombola from 14:30 to 15:00 (clue 3), and Raj's photo shows her behind the tombola table at 14:41, bending down to the box (clue 5).", "Kerry was serving cakes from 14:38 to 14:55 (clue 4), so Sandra was alone at the tombola.", "At 14:47 the caretaker's camera shows Sandra putting a big bag in the boot of her car (clue 6)."], "cleared": ["<b>Kerry</b> was selling cakes at 14:38, 14:46 and 14:55 (clue 4).", "<b>Owen</b> showed the console at 14:28 and handed over (clues 3 and 5).", "<b>Raj</b>, <b>Mr Ford</b> and <b>Mrs Clarke</b> only report what they saw."]}}, {"slug": "the-library-first-edition", "level": 1, "crime": "Theft", "who": "thief", "title": "The Library First Edition", "teaser": "A signed first edition vanishes from a locked library cabinet. Three people had a key – and one forgot which day the library is closed.", "intro": "At <b>Kingsford Library</b>, a signed first edition worth £4,000 has gone from the locked Local History cabinet. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.", "intro_text": "At Kingsford Library, a signed first edition worth £4,000 has gone from the locked Local History cabinet. Find all 6 clues, compare the statements and the evidence, and work out who did it.",